sy} :question/id #uuid "fdf659d7-2ff6-5274-9913-97ffa0cf4e09" :question/math-academy-id "q-223456" :question/problem "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $7?$\n\nI. $476$\n\nII. $732$\n\nIII. $423$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To check if a number is divisible by $7,$ double the last digit, subtract the result from the remaining digits, and then check if the difference is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $476,$ we have that \n\n$$\n47-2(6)=47-12=35\n$$\n\nwhich is divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $476$ is divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $732,$ we have that \n\n$$\n73-2(2)=73-4=69\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $732$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- For the number $423,$ we have that \n\n$$\n42-2(3)=42-6=36\n$$\n\nwhich is not divisible by $7.$ Therefore, $423$ is not divisible by $7.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee1838df-f1d6-5bc4-908c-b96e2ad577c9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Sets are Orthogonal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6083824-86d5-51f3-b347-2895e58da839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474816} {:answer/id #uuid "d6e8226e-0172-5d33-9eb5-ed8aacac25ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6083824-86d5-51f3-b347-2895e58da839" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474816} :answer-field/id #uuid "32a51cde-4bef-52b2-99da-b68e5b7cd2c8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475334} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16e1ada7-48ac-55ea-abdc-58511cd98079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474818} {:answer/id #uuid "937b8e9c-3d28-5737-8eed-9c803640fa7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16e1ada7-48ac-55ea-abdc-58511cd98079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474818} :answer-field/id #uuid "13bfc2a0-134b-5d27-9187-31d9b6d86aed" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475335} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04fb905e-e74d-5d79-b882-03aceed66713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474820} {:answer/id #uuid "dcf0a431-8efe-5df5-ab12-1ca33c633645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04fb905e-e74d-5d79-b882-03aceed66713" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474820} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad31b141-6411-5cf5-a477-5373690eb045" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475336}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9cc85c8f-2fc1-51b5-90b3-b4c40aaa9ac5" :question/math-academy-id "q-40288" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are orthogonal?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $U=\\{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}]\\}$\n\n- **II.** $V=\\{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\}$\n\n- **III.** $W=\\{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n$\\{{u}_{1},{u}_{2},{u}_{3}\\},$ \n$\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\},$ and \n$\\{{w}_{1},{w}_{2},{w}_{3}\\},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthogonal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,\\,{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0,\\,{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{3}=0.$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0.$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0,\\,{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0,\\,{w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{3}=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The set $U$ cannot be orthogonal since it contains  $3$ vectors from ${R}^{2}$ (in which we can have an orthogonal set with at most 2 non-zero vectors). Therefore, $U$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=0+10=10\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=12+3-1=14\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"None of the listed\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186433152 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133843 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee1838df-f1d6-5bc4-908c-b96e2ad577c9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Sets are Orthogonal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dfc814a-a2d7-57bf-9d56-49ce2fdf48c8" :answer/type 