d #uuid "c0e4d82f-21a7-54e9-a607-71112812ab73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474905} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ced5831-8921-5e8c-977b-762463a84003" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "34094a62-379f-5750-81e2-774654924818" :question/math-academy-id "q-80505" :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curve ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1.$ If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y), & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\nI. $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,1]$\n\nII. $R=[-1,1]\\times [0,1]$\n\nIII. $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](images/c5/c50e0e01d432b1db736fad09dd5f5b82286e981d88586e848d9b57c8a9910eb0.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y), & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangle II does not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangles I and III covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436043 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152200 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "100ab73e-3dad-5b15-9da2-d244c67bcc9b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Double Integrals Over Non-Rectangular Domains"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f989fd68-acf4-556b-8204-a65874853b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474954} {:answer/id #uuid "61629148-80cc-5f27-9e85-9aef3674ddb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f989fd68-acf4-556b-8204-a65874853b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474954} :answer-field/id #uuid "88f9ef63-a2d3-5377-8a45-034749a64a60" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475403} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "287515a8-f582-5ab7-b753-5427943347a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474956} {:answer/id #uuid "f0506c84-e3a0-5e51-8551-816cb0bfb600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0506c84-e3a0-5e51-8551-816cb0bfb600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474957} :answer-field/id #uuid "9792e7d3-778a-5703-9384-b40fab189daf" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475404} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48c73456-60c2-5847-b039-d9f5820e7f93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474958} {:answer/id #uuid "e3c1d1ec-df43-5584-85d8-8a2f435d0d68" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48c73456-60c2-5847-b039-d9f5820e7f93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474958} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab8930af-c48d-56c7-b380-3a5e38859878" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475405}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f7e910b3-a1a9-5ea8-8009-6cb31a154137" :question/math-academy-id "q-86864" :question/problem "![](images/bb/bbc1bc7b3bb910ffbd13571283bbfa305404d13eb2cb3b5ab423a1c02e46ab86.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true? \n\nI. ${∬}_{R}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-1,1]\\times [0,2]$\n\nII. ${∬}_{D}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,2]$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{D}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-1,2]\\times [-2,2]$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}), & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}y({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement II is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement III is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436527 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115243 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "853a04b2-591a-51c2-b80f-73f559355d9f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc959e6e-5194-5de1-a77f-64a4daedbf96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474750} {:answer/id #uuid "dda0ec43-a72d-5874-9f5d-834317bad33b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474751}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc959e6e-5194-5de1-a77f-64a4daedbf96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474750} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd81130a-839b-50b4-a531-a62146cb8917" :answer-field/key "D" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475301} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "126af85e-564c-5a88-83a5-7aa534682710" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474752} {:answer/id #uuid "a20e1d2b-1cc4-5391-9806-84714901dfaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474753}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a20e1d2b-1cc4-5391-9806-84714901dfaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474753} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6983834-6f71-5348-96c0-e1bdfc142faa" :answer-field/key "E" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475302} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b099eb91-9ca5-5c85-a7d5-72eff2354b80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474754} {:answer/id #uuid "263a88ac-61b5-5e85-ad17-92c76acc9730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b099eb91-9ca5-5c85-a7d5-72eff2354b80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474754} :answer-field/id #uuid "beaa7087-789c-5fc6-91c3-ada531bbfec4" :answer-field/key "F" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "73b54284-6d5f-5b76-a388-21fc0778bb8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-31889" :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,F=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $D$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\n- The matrix $E$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $F$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\nTherefore, only $E$ is an elementary matrix."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186436529 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115243 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "853a04b2-591a-51c2-b80f-73f559355d9f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Elementary 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f564662a-a586-5cf0-983d-a463cece18c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474828} {:answer/id #uuid "cd9ec697-d62c-5cd9-a7e3-d0be9a26170b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474829}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f564662a-a586-5cf0-983d-a463cece18c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474828} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c3c4731-0b36-5964-b452-fbb2af92efe4" :answer-field/key "M" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475340} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58c9ad47-9cc2-5588-b29e-efbaec72d300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474830} {:answer/id #uuid "6d6dd6fc-300a-5536-a4f8-6bf0bd3b7419" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58c9ad47-9cc2-5588-b29e-efbaec72d300" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474830} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f81fd52-e05c-55c9-8525-5b6cb62e9802" :answer-field/key "N" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475341} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c47f6210-eb6e-572b-8727-62ace0a342a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474832} {:answer/id #uuid "82ef391b-48b6-5a1e-b086-4012d85bb009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c47f6210-eb6e-572b-8727-62ace0a342a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474832} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c0c485d-839f-59be-8e63-a184b74dc721" :answer-field/key "P" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bb398bcb-fa77-5232-9d5f-318cb8cb3320" :question/math-academy-id "q-42704" :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,N=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,P=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrices $M$, $N$ and $P$ are not elementary matrices because they can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115252 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0303bd06-294e-5f7a-bbd2-b12abdeb93c5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Elementary 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3b342f7-479f-5bb5-b000-1997f2a94c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474840} {:answer/id #uuid "3add79aa-b544-598b-af4f-d5b4b279ff4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3add79aa-b544-598b-af4f-d5b4b279ff4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474841} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab74aaf1-327f-5fde-9c96-f2f46086aa4b" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475346} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2abd6a6-7c89-54d3-b70a-a21680d42074" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474842} {:answer/id #uuid "4302a6a2-4614-5a4f-aac7-608dbad07b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4302a6a2-4614-5a4f-aac7-608dbad07b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474843} :answer-field/id #uuid "39f49585-4fc8-5935-8bc0-98192f3f79bb" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475347} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fca8b313-642a-5d70-a829-f68ae8ad852a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474844} {:answer/id #uuid "ace9e31c-296b-54d6-b129-0f6d5b96d64d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474845}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fca8b313-642a-5d70-a829-f68ae8ad852a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474844} :answer-field/id #uuid "97cd03c8-e54c-548d-9f37-5495bf070383" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475348}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4f239bc7-130a-57fa-a436-9569195dcc53" :question/math-academy-id "q-43500" :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that an elementary matrix is obtained by performing exactly one elementary row operation on the identity matrix $I.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from $I$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from $I$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+6{R}_{3},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+6{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from $I$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are elementary matrices."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186437202 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115300 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "68350e0d-84ca-5b50-b05a-1bca3ceea40f" :knowledge-point/title "Transforming a 3x3 Matrix Into the Identity Matrix Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15d2eb39-b781-5d97-8e35-5f9e20e8b65d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474888} {:answer/id #uuid "bc949f57-4cf5-5c40-9977-23bea2b5a332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc949f57-4cf5-5c40-9977-23bea2b5a332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474889} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c72a4f1-56cb-5175-9a3e-52b6a59f0021" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475370} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe260ed2-664e-57fe-ad84-21fd62ea8d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474890} {:answer/id #uuid "7da7abf2-7bcd-52a2-904b-c23eb297f8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe260ed2-664e-57fe-ad84-21fd62ea8d94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474890} :answer-field/id #uuid "28ed5fa7-9c0f-5b9f-9432-2c4b214f12d8" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475371} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01f080db-7c5d-5102-946b-c423ad529aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474892} {:answer/id #uuid "108dcfb6-4aef-5c3a-869c-7adaa8d16bb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01f080db-7c5d-5102-946b-c423ad529aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474892} :answer-field/id #uuid "74b1e0b1-e76c-5a74-847a-91729de97d4f" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "67c5f653-7d0a-53ab-94d3-ce3b203a88ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-78776" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440655 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb02b67c-90d9-5baf-b00e-590e9271d89e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Closed Under Addition and Scalar Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d05376f6-1b0d-5d33-a541-3aa219c70c49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474380} {:answer/id #uuid "5c163f09-54be-5558-9c1e-fe94a54a1e20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d05376f6-1b0d-5d33-a541-3aa219c70c49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474380} :answer-field/id #uuid "40688437-da51-5c09-8938-382c42b205b5" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475116} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7e8cc97-462c-55aa-b04b-6dbb38612ce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474382} {:answer/id #uuid "15dd7df2-59de-5b51-b076-5c48eeebe741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7e8cc97-462c-55aa-b04b-6dbb38612ce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474382} :answer-field/id #uuid "0701114c-aa2e-546e-96ef-4e5405aa562a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475117} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fc0710a-c653-55e4-9d40-d1e8b67499c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474384} {:answer/id #uuid "e9124b17-545a-583b-9b07-99ee100d310e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474385}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fc0710a-c653-55e4-9d40-d1e8b67499c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186474384} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce028ac2-d2da-562a-87c9-ae46090732e5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475118}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c3d7a176-49a0-5f40-a976-fffa17513013" :question/math-academy-id "q-141158" :question/problem "Let $T$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ real matrices $A=({a}_{ij})$ such that ${a}_{11}{a}_{21}+{a}_{12}{a}_{22}>0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. The identity matrix ${I}_{2}$ belongs to $T.$\n\nII. For every $A\\in T$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha \\cdot A\\in T.$\n\nIII. The set is closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one at a time.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $T$ contains only matrices $A=({a}_{ij})$ such that ${a}_{11}{a}_{21}+{a}_{12}{a}_{22}>0.$ However, for the identity matrix ${I}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],$ we have ${a}_{11}{a}_{21}+{a}_{12}{a}_{22}=1\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 1=0≯0.$ So, ${I}_{2}\\notin T.$\n\n- Statement II is false. For example, let $\\alpha =0\\in R$ and $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]\\in T.$ Then, \n\n$$\n\\alpha \\cdot A=0\\cdot A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nwhere the sum of the products of columns' entries is $0\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 0=0≯0.$ Hence, $0\\cdot A\\notin T.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set is not closed under scalar multiplication.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""}]}
